-    <title>ARC System Will Be Unavailable for Use During Thanksgiving Week</title>
+    <title>The ARC System Will Be Unavailable for Use During Thanksgiving Week</title>
     <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="416" stream="IETF"/>
+    <author fullname="James C. Norton" initials="J. C." surname="Norton">
+      <organization showOnFrontPage="true">SRI-ARC</organization>
+      <address/>
+    </author>
     <date year="1972" month="November"/>
     <abstract pn="section-abstract">
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">The ARC PDP-10 system will be unavailable for ARC and NIC users from Friday, November 17 (6:00 pm PST ) through Sunday, November 26. (10:00 pm PST).  This will give our hardware team a period of nine days to work on equipment with a loss of only three SRI working days to users (Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday.)</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-2">This is the Network Information Center's notice to its network users of the schedule.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-3">In addition, a login message will be sent starting about 6 November to all users showing schedule.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-4">It will read something like: "THE ARC/NIC PDP-10 SYSTEM WILL BE UNAVAILABLE FOR USE FROM FRIDAY NOV 17 (6:00 pm PST) THRU SUNDAY NOV 26 (10:00 pm PST) FOR MAJOR HARDWARE WORK AS OUTLINED IN (12542,)".</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-5">For those who are interested, the hardware facility work to be done during this period will include:</t>
+      <ul spacing="normal" bare="false" empty="true" indent="3" pn="section-abstract-6">
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.1">Removal of the Bryant disk, Bryant disk controller and Cybernex drum-disk interference.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.2">Moving the Tasker display system and DEC dispack (old and new) equipment to their new locations.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.3">Having Bryant people run a combination drum maintenance and training session to teach ARC people how to change heads and clean the drum.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.4">Redoing the power cabling to the drum.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.5">Putting the new signal cable in between drum and controller.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.6">Debugging the parity checker.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.7">Making a check of all main signal levels in XCORE.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.8">Debugging the new cable from the parity checker to XCORE.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.9">Wiring the parity bit through the Cybernex XCORE interface.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.10">Getting any necessary power wiring done.</li>
+        <li pn="section-abstract-6.11">Building a wall for the next dispack location.</li>
+      </ul>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-7">[ This RFC was put into machine readable form for entry ]
+[ into the online RFC archives by BBN Corp. under the   ]
+[ direction of Alex McKenzie.                      1/97 ]</t>
     </abstract>
